# Prevent Cloudflare Pages from falling back to index.html for missing
# static assets. Without this, a stale browser referencing a prior
# build's JS hash (e.g. /assets/index-OLDHASH.js after a new deploy)
# gets the SPA fallback HTML instead of a 404 — and the browser's
# module-script strict-MIME check rejects the response with the error
#
#   Failed to load module script: Expected a JavaScript-or-Wasm module
#   script but the server responded with a MIME type of "text/html"
#
# leaving the user with a blank page until they hard-reload.
# Explicit 404 lets the browser retry + the SW's NetworkFirst pull a
# fresh index.html.

/assets/*  /404  404

# All other routes fall through to Cloudflare Pages' default static
# file serving, then the SPA index.html fallback.
